+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope; Correcting One Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Amends the NG-5 half of [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked, confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. That ADR named the path for reopening it: an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+Visits can be created but never corrected. A mistyped date or description stays on the pet's record. The owner decided at intake on 2026-10-24: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision.
+2. **Open amendment and cancellation together.** Rejected: the owner keeps cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope as REQ-VIS-003. Cancelling a booked visit stays a non-goal under NG-5. NG-4 is untouched: no visit is deleted.
+
+The owner also decided that the correction gains no visible entry point in this request: "the owner detail page gains no edit link in this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request."
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A correction replaces the visit's date and description; it never adds a second visit.
+- A correction passes the same checks as booking, so it must carry a date later than today. Whether a past visit may be corrected is an open question in the PRD.
+- A visible entry point to the correction needs a later owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — REQ-VIS-003.
